<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="google-site-verification" content="s2YUWbGP7cJsI6HUCKRX9YCtbVJVyA1Q1_jsNWj1RHc">
  <title>{{ title }} | HVTracker</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ description }}">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://hvtracker.net/blog/{{ slug }}/">

  <meta property="og:type" content="article">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ title }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ description }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://hvtracker.net/blog/{{ slug }}/">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://hvtracker.net/og-v2.png">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ title }}">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ description }}">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://hvtracker.net/og-v2.png">

  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ article_schema_json | safe }}</script>
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ faq_schema_json | safe }}</script>
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ breadcrumb_schema_json | safe }}</script>

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/site.css?v={{ css_hash }}">
  <style>
    body { font-size:16px; line-height:1.72; }
    a { color:var(--lobster); }
    .page { max-width:860px; padding:24px 20px 0; }
    .logo span { color:var(--lobster); }
    article { padding:34px 0 46px; }
    .eyebrow { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px; color:var(--lobster); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:1px; margin-bottom:12px; }
    h1 { font-size:34px; line-height:1.14; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:-0.02em; margin-bottom:12px; color:var(--ink); }
    .dek { color:var(--muted); font-size:17px; max-width:740px; }
    .meta { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); margin:18px 0 28px; }
    h2 { font-size:23px; line-height:1.25; margin:34px 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; color:var(--ink); }
    h3 { font-size:17px; margin:22px 0 8px; }
    p { margin-bottom:16px; }
    .summary {
      border-top:2px solid var(--lobster);
      padding:18px;
      background:var(--paper-2);
      margin:26px 0;
    }
    .summary strong { color:var(--moss); }
    .score-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2, 1fr); gap:14px; margin:24px 0; }
    .agent-card {
      border-top:2px solid var(--line-strong);
      padding:16px;
      background:var(--paper-2);
    }
    .agent-card h3 { margin-top:0; font-size:20px; }
    .score { font-family:var(--font-mono); color:var(--moss); font-size:30px; font-weight:700; line-height:1; }
    .rank { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); margin:6px 0 12px; }
    .facts { display:grid; gap:8px; margin-top:12px; }
    .fact { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:10px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding-top:8px; font-size:15px; }
    .fact span:first-child { color:var(--muted); }
    .fact span:last-child { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:13px; text-align:right; color:var(--ink); }
    table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:22px 0; font-size:15px; }
    th, td { border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:10px 8px; text-align:left; }
    th { color:var(--muted); font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; }
    td { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:13px; color:var(--ink); }
    td.win { color:var(--moss); font-weight:700; }
    .links { display:flex; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:26px; }
    .links a { border:1px solid var(--line); padding:9px 13px; color:var(--ink); background:var(--paper-2); font-size:13px; }
    .links a:hover { border-color:var(--lobster); color:var(--lobster); text-decoration:none; }
    .note { color:var(--muted); font-size:15px; }
    footer { padding:28px 0; border-top:1px solid var(--line); font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); text-align:center; }
    footer a { color:var(--lobster); }
    @media (max-width:720px) {
      h1 { font-size:26px; }
      .score-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    }
  </style>
  <!-- opt out: localStorage.setItem('hvt_notrack','1') -->
  <script>
    (function(){try{if(localStorage.getItem("hvt_notrack")==="1"){window["ga-disable-G-TZ8921LR0K"]=true;return}}catch(_){}
    var ua=navigator.userAgent||"";if(/HeadlessChrome|Puppeteer|Playwright|Claude\/[\d.]+.*Electron\/|bot|crawl|spider|curl|wget|python-requests/i.test(ua)){window["ga-disable-G-TZ8921LR0K"]=true}})();
  </script>
  <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-TZ8921LR0K"></script>
  <script>
    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
    gtag('js', new Date());
    gtag('config', 'G-TZ8921LR0K');
  </script>
  <script defer src="/analytics.js"></script>
</head>
<body data-page-type="blog_article" data-category="{{ category }}">
  {% include "_site_header.html.j2" %}
  <div class="page">

    <article>
      <div class="eyebrow">{{ category }} comparison</div>
      <h1>{{ h1 }}</h1>
      <p class="dek">{{ dek }}</p>
      <div class="meta">{{ date }} &middot; {{ read_time }} min read &middot; Data updated {{ updated }}</div>

      <div class="summary">
        <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> {{ winner.name }} currently leads {{ loser.name }} on HVTracker's evidence-weighted trust score: {{ winner.trust_score }} vs {{ loser.trust_score }}/100. This is not a popularity ranking; it combines supply-chain safety, identity/provenance, transparency, maintenance, and adoption signals.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="score-grid">
        {% for agent in [a, b] %}
        <section class="agent-card">
          <h3><a href="/agents/{{ agent.slug }}/">{{ agent.name }}</a></h3>
          <div class="score">{{ agent.trust_score }}</div>
          <div class="rank">#{{ agent.rank }} overall &middot; #{{ agent.category_rank }} in {{ category }} &middot; Grade {{ agent.evidence_grade }}</div>
          <p class="note">{{ agent.description or "No repository description available." }}</p>
          <div class="facts">
            <div class="fact"><span>Repository</span><span>{{ agent.display_repo or agent.repo }}</span></div>
            <div class="fact"><span>Stars</span><span>{{ agent.stars_fmt }}</span></div>
            <div class="fact"><span>Last push</span><span>{{ agent.last_push }}</span></div>
            <div class="fact"><span>Weekly commits</span><span>{{ agent.weekly_commits or 0 }}</span></div>
            <div class="fact"><span>Weekly downloads</span><span>{{ agent.downloads_fmt }}</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      <h2>{{ a.name }} vs {{ b.name }}: trust signal breakdown</h2>
      <p>Both projects are tracked in the <a href="/categories/{{ category_slug }}/">{{ category }}</a> category, but they do not expose the same evidence. The table below compares the public signals that feed HVTrust.</p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Signal</th><th>{{ a.name }}</th><th>{{ b.name }}</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>HVTrust score</th><td class="{{ 'win' if a.trust_score >= b.trust_score else '' }}">{{ a.trust_score }}</td><td class="{{ 'win' if b.trust_score > a.trust_score else '' }}">{{ b.trust_score }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Safety / Integrity</th><td class="{{ 'win' if a.trust_breakdown.safety >= b.trust_breakdown.safety else '' }}">{{ a.trust_breakdown.safety }}/30</td><td class="{{ 'win' if b.trust_breakdown.safety > a.trust_breakdown.safety else '' }}">{{ b.trust_breakdown.safety }}/30</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Identity / Provenance</th><td class="{{ 'win' if a.trust_breakdown.identity >= b.trust_breakdown.identity else '' }}">{{ a.trust_breakdown.identity }}/20</td><td class="{{ 'win' if b.trust_breakdown.identity > a.trust_breakdown.identity else '' }}">{{ b.trust_breakdown.identity }}/20</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Transparency</th><td class="{{ 'win' if a.trust_breakdown.transparency >= b.trust_breakdown.transparency else '' }}">{{ a.trust_breakdown.transparency }}/20</td><td class="{{ 'win' if b.trust_breakdown.transparency > a.trust_breakdown.transparency else '' }}">{{ b.trust_breakdown.transparency }}/20</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Maintenance</th><td class="{{ 'win' if a.trust_breakdown.maintenance >= b.trust_breakdown.maintenance else '' }}">{{ a.trust_breakdown.maintenance }}/20</td><td class="{{ 'win' if b.trust_breakdown.maintenance > a.trust_breakdown.maintenance else '' }}">{{ b.trust_breakdown.maintenance }}/20</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Adoption</th><td class="{{ 'win' if a.trust_breakdown.adoption >= b.trust_breakdown.adoption else '' }}">{{ a.trust_breakdown.adoption }}/10</td><td class="{{ 'win' if b.trust_breakdown.adoption > a.trust_breakdown.adoption else '' }}">{{ b.trust_breakdown.adoption }}/10</td></tr>
          <tr><th>OSSF Scorecard</th><td>{{ a.scorecard_fmt or "Unavailable" }}</td><td>{{ b.scorecard_fmt or "Unavailable" }}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Signed commits</th><td>{{ a.signed_commits_pct if a.signed_commits_pct is not none else "Unknown" }}{% if a.signed_commits_pct is not none %}%{% endif %}</td><td>{{ b.signed_commits_pct if b.signed_commits_pct is not none else "Unknown" }}{% if b.signed_commits_pct is not none %}%{% endif %}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Package provenance</th><td>{{ "Verified" if a.has_provenance else "Not detected" }}</td><td>{{ "Verified" if b.has_provenance else "Not detected" }}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Which one should you evaluate first?</h2>
      <p>If your priority is the most verifiable trust profile today, start with <a href="/agents/{{ winner.slug }}/">{{ winner.name }}</a>. It has the stronger current HVTrust score and ranks higher in {{ category }}. If your use case depends on a specific runtime, language, license, or integration model, use the individual profiles rather than the headline score alone.</p>

      <p>For production use, the practical checklist is: inspect the security policy, confirm package provenance or release signing where available, review recent maintenance cadence, and compare the exact trust breakdown. HVTracker is meant to reduce the first-pass research burden, not replace your own risk review.</p>

      <div class="links">
        <a href="/compare/{{ a.slug }}-vs-{{ b.slug }}/">Open side-by-side comparison</a>
        <a href="/agents/{{ a.slug }}/">{{ a.name }} profile</a>
        <a href="/agents/{{ b.slug }}/">{{ b.name }} profile</a>
        <a href="/categories/{{ category_slug }}/">All {{ category }}</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <footer>
      <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/spec/">Specifications</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/data/">Data API</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/compare/">Compare</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/badges/">Badges</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/changelog/">Changelog</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://github.com/YugantM/hvtracker/issues/new?template=agent-listing.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Submit Agent</a>
      <span class="footer-sep">&middot;</span>
      <a href="https://github.com/YugantM/hvtracker" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
